
Hello,

We are deploying Apigee Hybrid 1.17 on OpenShift (ROKS / IBM Cloud) in an enterprise environment where all outbound HTTPS traffic goes through a corporate forward proxy (HTTP scheme) that performs SSL/TLS interception.

The guardrails pod and operator pods fail with:

tls: failed to verify certificate: x509: certificate signed by unknown authority

Our httpProxy configuration in values:

yaml
httpProxy:
  host: "10.254.122.73"
  port: "3131"
  scheme: "http"

The proxy re-signs all HTTPS responses with a corporate CA certificate. The pods do not trust this CA.

Our question: What is the supported/recommended way to make the apigee-operator pods (guardrails hook, controller-manager) trust a custom CA certificate, without forking the Helm chart templates?

Specifically:

Is there a configuration property we may have missed (e.g. under httpProxy or elsewhere in the config property reference) to specify a custom CA bundle?
Is there a supported way to use extraVolumes/extraVolumeMounts on the operator chart?
Should we inject the CA at the node/cluster level instead (e.g. OpenShift MachineConfig to add the CA to the node trust store)?
Is there another recommended approach for environments with SSL-intercepting proxies?

We currently work around this by modifying the guardrails template to mount a ConfigMap with the corporate CA, but this is not sustainable across upgrades and we would like to use a supported method.

Environment:

Apigee Hybrid 1.17 (Helm-based install)
OpenShift 4.x (ROKS, IBM Cloud)
Deployment via ArgoCD (GitOps)
Forward proxy: HTTP scheme, performs MITM/SSL interception

Thank you.
